Installing PDFCube
==================

Requirements
------------

PDFCube requires a C++20 compiler, Meson 1.3 or newer, Ninja, GTK 4.12 or
newer, Poppler GLib 22.0 or newer, Cairo, libepoxy, and Boost Program Options.
The renderer supports desktop OpenGL and OpenGL ES 3 contexts.
Linux tests use Python 3, Pillow, EGL development headers, DejaVu fonts,
dbus-run-session, and a software OpenGL driver such as Mesa DRI. Transition
frames use surfaceless EGL; the GTK integration smoke test uses Xvfb and Xauth.
See tests/README.md for the test contract. Windows builds use
the MSYS2 UCRT64 GTK, Poppler, libepoxy, and Boost packages. macOS builds use
their Homebrew equivalents.

Build and test
--------------

    meson setup build --buildtype=release
    meson compile -C build
    meson test -C build --print-errorlogs

Installation
------------

The default prefix is /usr/local:

    sudo meson install -C build

Choose another prefix when configuring, for example:

    meson setup build --prefix=/opt/pdfcube --buildtype=release

Packagers can stage an installation without root access:

    DESTDIR=/tmp/pdfcube-stage meson install -C build

Uninstallation
--------------

Meson records installed files in the build directory:

    sudo ninja -C build uninstall

Reconfiguration
---------------

Change build options with `meson configure build`. To start from a clean
configuration, remove the build directory and run `meson setup` again.
